From a5ccee869143509ba5353d871b31004572b78749 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Giunta <marco_giunta@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:06:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] HID: Add driver for Lenovo Legion Spectrum keyboard
 backlight

Certain Lenovo Legion Gen 10 laptops, such as the Legion Pro 7 16AFR10H,
drive the keyboard backlight with an ITE 8258 USB controller (048d:c197),
which also hosts the internal keyboard.
The firmware's ACPI and WMI keyboard backlight methods are stubs on
these machines, so the backlight is currently not exposed to userspace
by the ideapad-laptop driver.

Add a driver exposing the brightness as the legion::kbd_backlight LED
class device, using the controller's vendor feature report. The LED
offers off plus the three levels used by the firmware's Fn+Up/Down
hotkeys (hardware values 0, 3, 6 and 9).

Per-key RGB and effects are left to userspace via hidraw.

The protocol was reverse-engineered by the LenovoLegionToolkit
project [1].

[1] https://github.com/LenovoLegionToolkit-Team/LenovoLegionToolkit

Signed-off-by: Marco Giunta <marco_giunta@outlook.it>
---
 drivers/hid/Kconfig                      |  12 ++
 drivers/hid/Makefile                     |   1 +
 drivers/hid/hid-ids.h                    |   1 +
 drivers/hid/hid-lenovo-legion-spectrum.c | 243 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 257 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/hid/hid-lenovo-legion-spectrum.c

